There are two errors at play here:

* The file upload widget from the Beehive side encodes uploaded files as a base64 data url. So it’s a base64-encoded string with the following prefix: {{data:application/pdf;base64,}}
* The file contents is then passed as is to {{/beehive/beehiveTask/storeDriverTaskResult}}
* The file is then decoded with {{Buffer.from(..., "base64")}} which then decodes the whole string, including the prefix
* The prefix itself is not base64-compatible, yet {{Buffer.from}} as implemented by node silently ignores the characters not in range. This is a known issue: [https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/8569|https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/8569|smart-link]

Customer Support are dealing with a similar contract. This is how they handle the file:

{noformat}        const pureBase64File = file.body_base64.replace(/^data:(.*);base64,/, "");
        const buffer = Buffer.from(pureBase64File, "base64");{noformat}

