Answers below - 

* *Can you confirm this arrangement is strictly leveraging on Work Profile?* I see amendments by EY as if Business account is included - see in the [preamble, also e.g. 1.9, 1.10, 2.6, 2.7.5, 3, 13.8.2, appendix 1|https://docs.google.com/document/d/13dZwOGKN6JrW7FfTDA-TUwOwQ8XtQVd6/edit]. This goes throughout the doc basically. If indeed there is some way how Work Profile and Business account would work together here then please elaborate as it would be first such setup I’m aware of; {color:#ff5630}*Yes the setup will just be work profile. We originally demo’ed both options (Business Account vs Work Profile) which may be why he’s referenced the online business account from a reporting perspective. But he’s aware the dashboard won’t show live WP data and this needs to be provided manually.*{color}
* Does EY (or their legal counsel) acknowledge that we have a separate agreement with the (app) users aka passengers which is fully independent from EY and this agreement? That includes the use of Work Profile, also payments (user can add their personal or EY provided card or whatnot to benefit from in-app payments). How EY-provided cards can and should be used is between EY and its users, and sits outside this agreement. See foremost [section 2, 3.2|https://docs.google.com/document/d/13dZwOGKN6JrW7FfTDA-TUwOwQ8XtQVd6/edit]. *I assume the object of this agreement is to just leverage on Work Profile for reporting so that it was more convenient for EY to monitor usage?* {color:#ff5630}*Correct - also better pricing and service via  the rebate and SLAs in appendix 1&2.*{color}
* *Bolt’s liability for driver partners - a classic.* C. [2.7.1, 7, 9.2|https://docs.google.com/document/d/13dZwOGKN6JrW7FfTDA-TUwOwQ8XtQVd6/edit]. Afaik we have never accepted liability for driver partners in an agency model market (which means vast majority of our markets) as it fundamentally goes against the whole narrative of how we operate. Regardless of how big or small the customer. It comes down to explaining the procedures we have in place to ensure drivers comply with our platform T&Cs, the applicable safety features, and how driver insurance responds to any possible claims. See some explanations and a supporting draft clause very below for inspiration. If indeed no luck then I suggest to escalate to Nick to see whether and how far he would be willing to sponsor changing the current practice. Recently similar issue was raised to management in Sweden for unlocking B2G deals but total value was ca 25M. It’s a principal risk/business decision not so much subject to a one-off legal approval. {color:#ff5630}*Thanks for drafting an explanation for this response - I’m happy to amend based on your advice and then include this explanation in the email reply to EY.*{color}

Once above cleared we also have several annexes subject to review by you yourself (appendix 1, 2), InfoSec (appendix 5). {color:#ff5630}*Noted - for Appendix 1 (the rebate), EY has advised we need to rebate each cost centre (in each country) so the admin of doing this on an annual basis likely won’t be worth it. I am working on an alternative rebate structure and once aligned with them will advise putting this into the contract.*{color}

Also, in the light of the above I think my participation on the Tuesday’s call is premature. Do let me know though if there’s anything where I should be included to discuss at this point. {color:#ff5630}*Makes sense - might be worth a quick internal call once I’ve confirmed an alternative rebate model and then we can fire this off to EY for feedback.* {color}

{color:#ff5630}*Cheers*{color}{color:#ff5630}! {color}

